# Ignore rules for this folder.
#
# THIS is the published repo. Whatever lands here goes to GitHub Pages under
# your own name, and you cannot un-publish a secret once it is in a pushed
# commit - deleting the file afterwards does not undo it. These rules are the
# cheap insurance against a careless `git add -A`.

# Secrets. Never. Not once.
.env
*.env
*token*.txt
*token*.json
.git-credentials
credentials.json
mcp_secrets.json
*secret*.json
*secret*.txt
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.ssh/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Browser builds and scratch
ms-playwright/
.playwright-mcp/
browser-profile/

# Build output, logs, OS junk
dist/
build/
logs/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Archives. Not content you serve.
*.zip
*.7z

# Media is NOT ignored on purpose - the website shelf tells you to use <img>,
# <audio> and <video>, so blocking those formats here would contradict it.
# The real limit is size: GitHub refuses a single file over 100 MB and pages
# over it get slow, and every byte stays in history forever even after you
# delete it. Resize stills, keep clips short, and compress before committing.
